<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1920</h1><p class="ref-lede">1920 in world history: 74 events, 20 births, 27 deaths, 3 works, 25 states founded and 25 that came to an end. 759 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1916">1916</a><a href="/years/1917">1917</a><a href="/years/1918">1918</a><a href="/years/1919">1919</a><a href="/years/1920" aria-current="page">1920</a><a href="/years/1921">1921</a><a href="/years/1922">1922</a><a href="/years/1923">1923</a><a href="/years/1924">1924</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Palmer Raids sweep up thousands of suspected radicals</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Federal agents directed by Attorney General A. Mitchell Palmer arrested thousands of suspected communists and anarchists in cities across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The raids marked the height of the first Red Scare.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-10">10 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">League of Nations comes into existence</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a> came into force, and with it the Covenant of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a>, the first permanent organisation for keeping world peace. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> never joined.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-16">16 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">League of Nations Council holds its first meeting</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The League's Council met for the first time in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, at the French Foreign Ministry. The League settled some minor disputes but failed to stop aggression in the 1930s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-23">23 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Netherlands refuses to hand over Kaiser Wilhelm II</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> government rejected Allied demands to extradite the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-emperor">German Emperor</a> for trial under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a>. Wilhelm lived in exile at Doorn until his death in 1941.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-1">1 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Royal Canadian Mounted Police is formed</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Royal North-West Mounted Police merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> Police to form the RCMP, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s national police force. Its scarlet tunics became one of the country's best-known symbols.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/canada">Canada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-24">24 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hitler presents the Nazi Party's 25-point programme</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Hofbräuhaus in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>, Hitler read out the programme of the German Workers' Party, which renamed itself the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">National Socialist German Workers' Party</a> (NSDAP) around this time.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-18">18 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tennessee ratifies the 19th Amendment, giving US women the vote</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> became the 36th state to ratify, by one vote cast by a young legislator heeding his mother's letter. The amendment barred denial of the vote on account of sex.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-26">26 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The 19th Amendment is certified, giving US women the vote</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretary of State Bainbridge Colby certified the 19th Amendment, barring denial of the vote on account of sex. It crowned a campaign launched at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seneca-people">Seneca</a> Falls in 1848.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rapallo-1920" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rapallo-1920.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-12">12 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Italy and Yugoslavia settle their border in the Treaty of Rapallo</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> signed the Treaty of Rapallo, settling their post-war border. Italy received Istria, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zara</a> and several islands, the rest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> went to the Yugoslav kingdom, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rijeka">Fiume</a> became a free state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rapallo-1920">Treaty of Rapallo (1920)</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-15">15 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The League of Nations holds its first Assembly</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 41 nations met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> for the first Assembly of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a>. Weakened by the absence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the League failed to prevent the aggression of the 1930s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-21">21 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bloody Sunday in Dublin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-collins">Michael Collins</a>'s IRA squad killed 14 men, mostly British intelligence officers, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> that morning. In the afternoon, Crown forces fired on the crowd at a Gaelic football match in Croke Park, killing 14 civilians.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-trianon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-trianon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-trianon">Treaty of Trianon</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Trianon was the peace treaty signed on 4 June 1920 at the Grand Trianon palace in Versailles between the Allied powers and Hungary after the First World War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-sevres">Treaty of Sèvres</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Sèvres was the peace treaty of 1920 between the Allied powers and the Ottoman Empire after the First World War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maysalun" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-maysalun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maysalun">Battle of Maysalun</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Maysalun was fought on 24 July 1920 at the Maysalun pass west of Damascus between French forces under General Mariano Goybet and a small Syrian army led by the war minister Yusuf al-Azma.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kapp-putsch" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kapp-putsch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/kapp-putsch">Kapp Putsch</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Kapp Putsch was an attempted coup against the Weimar Republic in March 1920, led by Wolfgang Kapp and General Walther von Lüttwitz with Freikorps troops due to be disbanded under the Treaty of Versailles.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-war">Polish–Lithuanian War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Polish–Lithuanian War was an undeclared conflict of 1920 between Poland and Lithuania over the Vilnius region.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/soviet-lithuanian-peace-treaty">Soviet–Lithuanian Peace Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet–Lithuanian Peace Treaty was signed in Moscow on 12 July 1920, ending the war between Soviet Russia and Lithuania.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/san-remo-conference" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-remo-conference.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/san-remo-conference">San Remo conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The San Remo conference was a meeting of the Allied Supreme Council held at Sanremo in Italy in April 1920.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-giedraiciai">Battle of Giedraičiai</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Giedraičiai was fought on 19–21 November 1920 around Giedraičiai, north of Vilnius, where Lithuanian forces defeated troops of Lucjan Żeligowski, who had seized Vilnius for Poland the month before.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-warsaw-1920">Battle of Warsaw (1920)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Warsaw was fought in August 1920 during the Polish–Soviet War, when Polish forces under Józef Piłsudski counter-attacked the Red Army advancing on the Polish capital.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-seeb">Treaty of Seeb</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Seeb was an agreement concluded in 1920, through British mediation, between the Sultan of Muscat and the tribal leaders of the Ibadi Imamate of Oman in the interior.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tartu-russian-estonian" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tartu-russian-estonian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tartu-russian-estonian">Treaty of Tartu (Russian–Estonian)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Tartu was signed on 2 February 1920 between the Republic of Estonia and Soviet Russia, ending the Estonian War of Independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-lushnje">Congress of Lushnjë</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Congress of Lushnjë was a national assembly of Albanian delegates held at Lushnjë from 28 to 31 January 1920.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tartu-finland-russia">Treaty of Tartu (Finland–Russia)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Tartu between Finland and Soviet Russia, signed on 14 October 1920 in the Estonian town of Tartu, fixed the border between the two states after the Finnish Civil War and the volunteer expeditions into Russian territory.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/turkish-armenian-war">Turkish–Armenian War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Turkish–Armenian War was fought from September to December 1920 between the Turkish nationalist forces of the Grand National Assembly and the First Republic of Armenia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/franco-syrian-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-syrian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/franco-syrian-war">Franco-Syrian War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Franco-Syrian War was a short conflict in 1920 between France and the Arab Kingdom of Syria proclaimed under Faisal I.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/plan-of-agua-prieta">Plan of Agua Prieta</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Plan of Agua Prieta was the revolt proclaimed in April 1920 at Agua Prieta, Sonora, by supporters of Álvaro Obregón against President Venustiano Carranza.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sirvintos">Battle of Širvintos</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Širvintos was fought on 17–21 November 1920 near the town of Širvintos, north-west of Vilnius, between Lithuanian forces and the Polish troops of Lucjan Żeligowski, who had seized Vilnius in October.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bloody-christmas-1920">Bloody Christmas (1920)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Bloody Christmas was the Italian army and navy attack on Fiume, now Rijeka, from 24 to 29 December 1920, ending Gabriele D'Annunzio's occupation of the city.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tartu-finnish-russian">Treaty of Tartu (Finnish–Russian)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Tartu was signed on 14 October 1920 between Finland and Soviet Russia, confirming the border between the two states after Finnish independence.</p></div></li></ol></section>
