<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-sfsr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20SFSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian SFSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Red Army defeats Wrangel’s last White army in Crimea</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Polish forces seize Vilnius; Kaunas becomes the temporary capital</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Estonia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Estonia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Treaty of Tartu ends the War of Independence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Latvia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Latvia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A peace treaty with Soviet Russia recognises Latvian independence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/classical-chinese"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Classical%20Chinese.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Classical Chinese</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">China’s Ministry of Education orders primary schools to teach the vernacular instead of Classical Chinese</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/womens-suffrage-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Women's%20suffrage%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Women's suffrage movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Nineteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution is ratified</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mandatory-palestine"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mandatory%20Palestine.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mandatory Palestine</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A British civilian administration under High Commissioner Sir Herbert Samuel replaces military rule in July; riots in Jerusalem in April have killed five Jews and four Arabs.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-cuba-1902-1959"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Cuba%20(1902-1959).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Cuba (1902-1959)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sugar prices peak and crash in the Dance of the Millions, ruining the country financially and strengthening foreign investors.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/joan-of-arc"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Joan%20of%20Arc.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Joan of Arc</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Canonized by Pope Benedict XV</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/free-state-of-prussia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Free%20State%20of%20Prussia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Free State of Prussia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Kapp Putsch collapses after six days; Otto Braun becomes minister president and the constitution is adopted on 30 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania-1918-1940"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania%20(1918-1940).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania (1918-1940)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Soviet–Lithuanian Peace Treaty is signed, and in October Żeligowski's Mutiny takes Vilnius</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/weimar-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Weimar%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Weimar Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Kapp Putsch fails after a general strike and the refusal of the bureaucracy to obey Kapp</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/armenian-ssr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Armenian%20SSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Armenian SSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 29 November Soviet Armenia is established as the 11th Red Army enters and the government of the First Republic hands power to the Bolsheviks</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Hungary%20(1920-1946).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A coalition of right-wing forces restores the monarchy, and Miklós Horthy is chosen regent on 1 March</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Hungary%20(1920-1946).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hungary signs the Treaty of Trianon on 4 June, losing Transylvania, much of Upper Hungary and Vojvodina</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/korea-under-japanese-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Korea%20under%20Japanese%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Korea under Japanese rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independence forces under Kim Chwajin and Hong kill about 1,500 Japanese soldiers at the Battle of Cheongsanri, and the Imperial Japanese Army retaliates with the Gando massacre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/ho-chi-minh"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ho%20Chi%20Minh.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ho Chi Minh</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Votes for the Third International at the Congress of Tours and becomes a founding member of the French Communist Party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Warsaw%20(1920).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Warsaw (1920)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Semyon Budyonny's 1st Cavalry Army breaks through the Polish lines and all Polish fronts collapse</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Warsaw%20(1920).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Warsaw (1920)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tukhachevsky's Western Front begins an all-out assault in Belarus and reaches Białystok on 28 July</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Warsaw%20(1920).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Warsaw (1920)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Piłsudski conceives a revised plan at the Belweder Palace on the night of 5 to 6 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Warsaw%20(1920).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Warsaw (1920)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The final Soviet assault on Warsaw begins on 12 August with the attack on the Praga bridgehead and at Radzymin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Warsaw%20(1920).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Warsaw (1920)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Piłsudski's Task Force begins its march north from the Wieprz River on 16 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Warsaw%20(1920).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Warsaw (1920)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Polish army defeats the Red Army again at the Battle of the Niemen River, fought from 15 to 21 September</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-warsaw-1920"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Warsaw%20(1920).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Warsaw (1920)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A ceasefire is signed on 12 October under pressure from France and Britain, and the fighting ends by 18 October</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/berlin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Berlin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Berlin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Greater Berlin Act incorporates surrounding towns and villages and roughly doubles the population</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/damascus"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Damascus.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Damascus</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A French army enters Damascus, which becomes the capital of the Mandate for Syria</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/aleppo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aleppo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aleppo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The French declare the State of Aleppo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/bukhara"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bukhara.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bukhara</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Red Army troops under Mikhail Frunze attack the city, and the emir flees</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/the-communist-manifesto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/The%20Communist%20Manifesto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>The Communist Manifesto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first Chinese printing is distributed, funded by Grigori Voitinsky and translated by Chen Wangdao</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/cyrus-cylinder"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Cyrus%20Cylinder.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Cyrus Cylinder</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">J. B. Nies of Yale University published the text of the smaller fragment, B</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/surrealism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Surrealism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Surrealism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Breton and Soupault publish The Magnetic Fields, written with automatic techniques</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/temperance-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Temperance%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Temperance movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Eighteenth Amendment introduces prohibition of the manufacture, sale and distribution of alcoholic beverages in the United States</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/nazism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The party is renamed the National Socialist German Workers’ Party to appeal to left-wing workers, a change Hitler at first opposed</span></li></ul></section>
